<!-- awf:section positioning -->
# {{ .prefix }}-subagent-driven-development

The subagent implementation chain iterates phases. It preserves sequential implementation dispatch and exclusive implementation-tool batching.

<!-- awf:include plan-flexibility -->
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section per-task-review-note -->
**Phase review is report-only.** The parent settles findings after the phase-closing commit.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section when-to-invoke -->
## When to invoke

Invoke when a plan phase benefits from delegated implementation. A plan may mix modes; delegated execution never delegates transaction ownership, so hand inline phases to `{{ .prefix }}-executing-plans`.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section procedure-resolve-plan -->
## Procedure
<!-- awf:include outline-approval -->

1. Resolve the mutable plan and read every declared phase mode. This skill may run without an effort. If continuity independently fired, validate its immutable slug and exact `.awf/efforts/<slug>/memory.md`, confirm canonical YAML `effort: <slug>`, preserve one user-managed writer, and use the managed worktree when present; otherwise omit effort and memory fields from dispatches and checkpoints. If changed facts newly make continuity useful, invoke `{{ if index .skills "effort-workflow" }}{{ .prefix }}-effort-workflow{{ else }}the effort lifecycle owner{{ end }}` before further mutation. Repository authority remains primary, and standalone memory is forbidden.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section procedure-raise-concerns -->
2. You, the dispatching parent, resolve missing phase context, paths, boundaries, checks, or a closing subject when repository authority determines a compliant detail; use the shared authority boundary for a genuine unresolved design fork. Never hand a child an incomplete phase and let it discover the gap.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section procedure-extract-context -->
3. Per `{{ .layout.maintainableCodeDesign }}`, preserve the plan's settled durable choices, including a bounded enabling refactor; reassess them if grounded source contradicts them and stop and escalate rather than accept a bolt-on workaround.
<!-- awf:include clean-integration -->
<!-- awf:include implementation-autonomy -->
Extract the complete phase: goal, ordered tasks, exact paths, semantic boundary and ownership, external/internal representations and their translation point, allowed dependency direction, preparatory-refactor decision, prohibited bolt-on shortcuts, validation expectations, dependencies, prior phase commits, checks, closing subject, and the phase's batch of the ADR's declared State changes operations (V2). The owner runs `./awf context <the phase's exact paths>` before editing.
<!-- awf:include context-spill -->
The owner preserves the settled durable design or reports invalidating source facts; does not replan, broaden the task, or perform unrelated cleanup.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section dispatch-conventions -->
4. For a `subagent-driven` phase, the parent verifies a known clean and green baseline. A fresh parent may run `./awf read plan <plan> <P>` for the executable closure. A task projection's generated scope notice, Phase close, and Advances/Completes outcomes are phase-owner context only; they never transfer commit, review, checkpoint, handoff, helper, or outcome authority; projection changes neither ownership nor checkpoint boundaries. Call one commit-disabled implementation child alone in its parent tool batch{{ if .targetSubagentTools }}. Effort-backed pre-integration implementation dispatches supply the managed-worktree path as `verificationCheckout`, while effort-free or root-owned work intentionally omits it. The validated checkout is both the child CWD and before-and-after HEAD identity. The main Pi session remains at the project root, so parent mutations name managed-worktree paths explicitly. Child CWD alignment is not filesystem confinement. Governed primary-checkout lifecycle transitions remain at the primary checkout.{{ end }} Then provide the complete phase, explicitly identify the parent-supplied approved boundary, and, when an effort exists, provide its slug and exact owned memory path. The child is the `implementer` agent and returns its closed focused-evidence receipt; it never edits parent memory. {{ if .targetSubagentTools }}Choose the smallest reliable tier - `small` (narrow, mechanical), `standard` (substantive but bounded), or `large` (broad, intricate, cross-cutting, or high-consequence) - escalating after uncertainty, failed reasoning, or widened scope; omit the `model` field to use configured role routing, overriding deliberately with the tier's exact `provider/model-id`. Never pass `default`, `auto`, or `inherit parent` as a model value. Full tier definitions: docs/workflow.md.{{ else }}Choose the smallest reliable tier - `small` (narrow, mechanical), `standard` (substantive but bounded), or `large` (broad, intricate, cross-cutting, or high-consequence) - escalating after uncertainty, failed reasoning, or widened scope; select the smallest reliable target-native model explicitly, or use the harness default and note in the dispatch brief that explicit selection is unavailable. Full tier definitions: docs/workflow.md.{{ end }} The parent independently inventories the checkout, rejects writes outside the delegated boundary, confirms the reported unchanged HEAD and end state, and integrates the result. The parent stages the complete transaction explicitly and creates the declared phase-closing commit only after `./awf check staged` and {{ with .vars.gateCmd }}`{{ . }}`{{ else }}the project's gate{{ end }} pass; a wired pre-commit hook enforces both at commit time, and the parent runs them manually first only in a clone without wired hooks (checkable with `git config core.hooksPath`; when in doubt, run both manually). The parent also owns terminal exhaustive verification. A child receipt never substitutes for a parent gate. Never dispatch concurrent implementation children.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section procedure-status-handling -->
5. Before review, inventory the completed child receipt, verify that it names the intended worktree and unchanged HEAD, and confirm the parent-owned phase-closing commit as the branch tip with `git status --short` empty. Build the phase-review brief with that exact commit, the complete phase scope, child focused evidence plus parent verification results, and the verbatim deviation report. Dispatch one report-only phase review through correctness, plan/authority, documentation, and maintainability lenses. Require its structured coverage summary to return the exact phase-closing commit, reviewed scope and range, verification results, verbatim deviation report, freshness against the current branch tip, and any unreviewed settlement. The parent owns this transient evidence and revalidates its commit, range, and branch-tip freshness before reuse. {{ if .targetSubagentTools }}Choose the smallest reliable tier - `small` (narrow, mechanical), `standard` (substantive but bounded), or `large` (broad, intricate, cross-cutting, or high-consequence) - escalating after uncertainty, failed reasoning, or widened scope; omit the `model` field to use configured role routing, overriding deliberately with the tier's exact `provider/model-id`. Never pass `default`, `auto`, or `inherit parent` as a model value. Full tier definitions: docs/workflow.md.{{ else }}Choose the smallest reliable tier - `small` (narrow, mechanical), `standard` (substantive but bounded), or `large` (broad, intricate, cross-cutting, or high-consequence) - escalating after uncertainty, failed reasoning, or widened scope; select the smallest reliable target-native model explicitly, or use the harness default and note in the dispatch brief that explicit selection is unavailable. Full tier definitions: docs/workflow.md.{{ end }} When deviations or findings exist, the parent lands one focused post-review settlement commit containing plan Notes reconciliation and mechanical or reasoned review fixes before checkpointing or later execution; it never rewrites the parent-owned phase-closing commit. A no-deviation, no-finding phase needs no empty settlement commit. The parent owns focused settlement commits and may append only a concise advisory observation to memory. Evidence loss after context loss, session replacement, or effort-free continuation, or any unverifiable freshness, falls back to ordinary terminal review. Divergence, changed authority, reasoned post-review fixes, or any material mutation invalidates affected coverage and triggers renewed review; the report-only reviewer never edits memory.

<!-- awf:include checkpoint-routine -->
<!-- awf:include phase-loop-continuation -->

If an implementation child stops dirty, inventory `git status --short`, diff, completed and remaining work, and failed checks. Choose parent completion, restore the known green baseline and redispatch the complete revised phase, or stop for user input. An explicit transfer carries the complete revised phase, dirty-state inventory, completed and remaining work, and recovery verification; a blind successor instruction for one task is forbidden.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section per-task-review -->
6. Review is report-only and phase-level; review fixes remain parent-owned and do not recreate the original transaction.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section final-task-adr-flip -->
7. Apply every explicit V2 batch, including the final batch, atomically with matching claims and lifecycle events in the owning phase. Do not flip terminal artifact status in a phase.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section terminal-step -->
8. After all settled phases, reuse only fresh phase coverage: a single phase reviews unreviewed settlement or integration, while multiple phases focus cross-phase composition, settlements, and integration. Always retain `./awf audit` over the complete final range, including settlement commits. Evaluate implementation-review need independently. Invoke `{{ .prefix }}-reviewing-impl` for meaningful breadth, non-obvious logic, contract or compatibility effects, migrations, security, concurrency, data-loss risk, verification requiring substantive judgment, or uncertainty. Skip it only for locally obvious, low-risk, directly verified work where independent review is unlikely to find meaningful hidden consequences. After assurance settles or is explicitly skipped, effort-backed work returns to `{{ if index .skills "effort-workflow" }}{{ .prefix }}-effort-workflow{{ else }}the effort lifecycle owner{{ end }}` for artifact closure. For effort-free work, the parent performs the deferred ADR/plan terminal transaction only after appending each closing Proposed plan's parsed Terminal reconciliation under Notes, using a full-SHA implementation range ending at current `HEAD`, the exact old and new touched paths accumulated across every selected commit including merge resolutions, and every material route deviation or exact `none`; an endpoint diff or prose markers cannot substitute. It applies only legal status transitions under `{{ .prefix }}-adr-lifecycle`, runs the required gate and audit, and concludes.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section notes -->
## Notes
- Sequential dispatch only, never parallel. Helpers remain sequential, commit-disabled, path-disjoint, and parent-integrated.
- Expected output is non-negotiable.
<!-- awf:end -->
<!-- awf:section red-flags -->
## Red flags

Do not casually dispatch over a dirty checkout, infer plan-wide mode, or let a helper own a shared file or closing commit.
<!-- awf:end -->
